  "title": "Nebuchadnezzar II",
  "summary": "Nebuchadnezzar II succeeded his father Nabopolassar as king of Babylon in 605 BCE and reigned until 562 BCE. His forces took Jerusalem in 597 BCE and, after a siege, burned and destroyed it, deporting its leading citizens; sources give 586 or 587 for that second capture. He rebuilt Babylon with walls, temples and palaces.",
